known_false_positives.description:
Bug: When `param_value` contains no '=' character, `rfind('=')` returns `std::string::npos`. Calling `substr(0, npos)` will throw `std::out_of_range` exception. Need to handle the case when `suffix_allowed` is true but no '=' exists in the string.

```suggestion
            const std::string param_value_hostport{
                suffix_allowed ? [&param_value]() {
                    const auto pos = param_value.rfind('=');
                    return pos == std::string::npos ? param_value : param_value.substr(0, pos);
                }() : param_value};
```
